      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PAY KEEPING (4) started big odds but ran a huge race last time when finishing 3rd over 520m at Wentworth Park (30.05)in NG. Scored at this track in weaker company the previous run. Form at the trip excellent including two wins. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings two times from four attempts. Sure to be about the mark. PRINCESS ADA (6) is struggling to break through but racing consistently, finishing in the minors six starts on end. Last time out flew the lids with a fast early sectional but gathered in and finished in the minors when third (26.27) at Bulli over 472m. Likely to be in the finish again. GRANT KEEPING (8) is worth forgiving for his last effort when fifth (29.87) at Wentworth Park over 520m. Should be in this for a long way. DO THE STOMP (2) is new to this trip but should be in the mix.",
